<title>SINGAPORE: Sembawang Maritime 1996 net up 81 pct.</title>
<headline>Sembawang Maritime 1996 net up 81 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 16.59    vs   9.16</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	    7.5     vs   5.0</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	16.9     vs   9.6</p>
<p>    Turnover		  173.50    vs 136.74</p>
<p>    Investment income	 0.47    vs   0.93</p>
<p>    Other income		8.95    vs   8.07</p>
<p>    Operating pre-tax	35.16    vs  24.37</p>
<p>    Interest expense	  3.34    vs   1.31</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     22.30    vs  19.76</p>
<p>    Associates		  9.25    vs   6.87</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	   28.18    vs  19.18</p>
<p>    Tax			   8.24    vs   5.26</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (3.35)   vs  (4.77)</p>
<p>Dividend pay/register: June 27, 1997/June 11, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Full name is Sembawang Maritime Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
